11. Docker Hub & Container Registries
A registry stores container images so they can be shared between development, CI/CD systems, and deployment
servers.
docker login
docker tag my-app:1.0 username/my-app:1.0
docker push username/my-app:1.0
docker pull username/my-app:1.0
A typical flow is: Build locally/CI → Tag image → Push to registry → Pull on deployment server → Run
container.
12. Complete Deployment Workflow
Step 1: Create application code and Dockerfile.
Step 2: Build the image.
docker build -t my-app:1.0 .
Step 3: Test locally.
docker run -d -p 3000:3000 --name my-app my-app:1.0
Step 4: Check container and logs.
docker ps
docker logs my-app
Step 5: Tag and push the image.
docker tag my-app:1.0 username/my-app:1.0
docker push username/my-app:1.0
Step 6: On the deployment server, pull the image.
